meditation is an extremely powerful tool  for developing focus and concentration  as well as for taking conscious control  over the physiological state to attain  self mastery while you might associate  meditation with self-help and relaxation  the truth is there's a lot more to it  than that it can be seriously badass did  you know that the samurai would  regularly meditate on the concept of  death this allowed them to become  desensitized to the subject such that  they could hurl themselves into battle  with no concern for their own physical  well-being tapping into greater strength  and reflexes with no fear pretty awesome  many people believe that coming to terms  with death this way can help them to  live their best lives now a Steve Jobs  said remembering that I'll be dead soon  as the most important tool I'll ever  encounter to help me make the big  choices in life because almost  everything all external expectations all  pride all fear of embarrassment or  failure these things just fall away in  the face of death leaving only what is  truly important remembering that you're  going to die is the best way I know to  avoid the trap of thinking you have  something to lose you are already naked  there is no reason not to follow your  heart powerful stuff this is an example  of using meditation for a purpose other  than relaxation and mindfulness most of  us have little notion of just how many  types of meditation there are or what  can be done with them meditation can  broadly be broken down into two types  Directive meditation and of  non-directive meditation most of us are  familiar with directive forms of  meditation  these include practices such as focusing  on breathing as in breath awareness  meditation an object as in gazing  meditation the body as in body scan  meditation or a word or mantra as in  Transcendental Meditation  we can also place meditations that aim  to clear the mind or disengage with  thoughts into this category that might  include many forms of mindfulness  meditation using this type of meditation  can help us to rise above anxious  thoughts and thus to develop emotional  resiliency they generally train us to be  more aware of what we're thinking of and  therefore to define our own mental state  and how we wish to respond to the world  around us in that regard mindfulness has  a lot in common with the philosophy of  stoicism it can form to developer  interoception  and our emotional intelligence  which is something I'll be talking about  in future on this channel many people  find that the act of meditation itself  is highly therapeutic by focusing  intently you can quiet activity in  unused brain areas thereby reducing  anxiety this can even lead to the  experience of ego death where you only  experience the present moment and lose  any sense of nagging doubt or insecurity  combined with calm breathing practices  this can be highly rejuvenating this is  an intensely relaxing process that may  represent a form of true relaxation that  we rarely engage in anymore many of us  now relax by shooting zombies and  worrying about work Shaolin warrior  monks believed strongly in the  importance of meditative practices such  as Qigong as a means to counterbalance  the effects of intense training if  you're feeling burned out and exhausted  you might need to consider the use of  recovery strategies such as these some  forms of meditation such as yoga nidra  have even been suggested as ways to  reduce the need for sleep that's  something I'll be talking about more on  this channel in future what this also  does is to develop focus  studies show that directive meditation  can help to develop the anterior  cingulate cortex a part of the brain  associated with sustained attention if  you need to write a long essay then  practicing meditation could help you to  achieve that this type of meditation  also increases IQ and appears to enhance  whole brain connectivity you can find  studies supporting these statements 